[Step 470] Q: Let $y=f(x)$ be an odd function. When $x < 0$, we have $f(x)=x^2+ax$, and $f(3)=6$. Find the value of $a$.
Ground truth: 5
Response[0]:
<start_working_out>
Since $f(x)$ is an odd function, $f(-x) = -f(x)$ for all $x$.
We are given that $f(3) = 6$. Since $3 > 0$, we have that $f(-3) = -6$.
Substituting $-3$ into $f(x) = x^2 + ax$, we get
$-3^2 + a(-3) = -6$ and simplifying this we have 
$9-3a=-6$ 
$3a=3$ 
$a=1$.
<end_working_out>
<SOLUTION>1</SOLUTION>
