To find the number of zeros of the function $g(x)=f(x)-2$, we first need to determine the expression for $g(x)$ based on the given function $f(x)$.

For $x\leq 1$, we have $f(x)=3-2x$.
So, $g(x)=f(x)-2=3-2x-2=1-2x$.

For $x>1$, we have $f(x)=x^2$.
So, $g(x)=f(x)-2=x^2-2$.

Now, to find the zeros of the function $g(x)$, we set both expressions equal to zero and solve for $x$.


