[Step 810] Q: Rob remembered the Eiffel Tower, which was the tallest structure in the world at the time it was built. The Eiffel Tower is lower than today's tallest man-made structure, the Burj Khalifa, by 506 m. I
Ground truth: 324
Response[0]:
<start_working_out>

To find the height of the Eiffel Tower, we can subtract the height difference between the Eiffel Tower and the Burj Khalifa from the height of the Burj Khalifa.

Height of Burj Khalifa = 830 m
Height difference = 506 m

Height of Eiffel Tower = Height of Burj Khalifa - Height difference
Height of Eiffel Tower = 830 m - 506 m
Height of Eiffel Tower = 324 m

